// title: Riddle Me This
// xp: 25
// hidden: is_palindrome #test("Gotham")[false]
// hidden: is_palindrome #test("A Toyota")[true]
// hint: The check is right for "abba", but the Riddler's riddles have capitals, spaces and punctuation.
// hint: Keep only the letters, all in one case, before comparing. `char` has a method that tells a letter, and lists have `filter` and `map`.
//
// The Riddler has left Gotham a stack of riddles, and every answer is a
// palindrome: a phrase that reads the same backwards, if you ignore
// capitals, spaces and punctuation. "Never odd or even" is one.
//
// `is_palindrome` only works on bare lowercase words. Fix it before
// Batman has to say it. (He will. He's Batman.)
#test("Never odd or even")[true]
#test("Was it a car or a cat I saw?")[true]
#test("Riddle me this")[false]
fun is_palindrome(s: str) -> bool {
    let cs = s.chars()
    return cs == cs.reversed()
}
